From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) init.common.rc: do not start netd

An explicit "start netd" clears the service's "disabled" flag, so this
early start in post-fs-data would bring netd up even though Sailfish OS
does not use it (see the system/netd change). dummy_netd provides the
netd binder service instead.
---
 rootdir/vendor/etc/init/hw/init.common.rc |    3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rootdir/vendor/etc/init/hw/init.common.rc b/rootdir/vendor/etc/init/hw/init.common.rc
index bab52ce42ecb10bb32f0f4e7590e6f65fb9c56b0..8d264a785167b68b5099cd7804d4da2829b1b823 100644
--- a/rootdir/vendor/etc/init/hw/init.common.rc
+++ b/rootdir/vendor/etc/init/hw/init.common.rc
@@ -134,9 +134,6 @@ on late-fs
     mount_all /vendor/etc/fstab.${ro.hardware} --late
 
 on post-fs-data
-    # We can start netd here before in is launched in common init.rc on zygote-start
-    start netd
-
     # Create directory used by bluetooth subsystem
     mkdir /data/vendor/bluetooth 2770 bluetooth bluetooth
 
